@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+# 9. Ticket assignment and notifications
+
+Date: 2026-11-15
+Status: Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+Agents need to take ownership of active tickets. The assignment must be visible through the API and operator tools,
+recorded in the audit log, and survive restarts. An agent taking a ticket should be notified without making the HTTP
+request depend on the notifier.
+
+## Decision
+
+We will store an `assignee` on every ticket. It is `null` when unassigned and otherwise a trimmed, non-empty, single-line
+agent name of at most 64 characters. Existing data files without this field load as unassigned, and the data-file version
+does not change.
+
+We will assign and unassign through `PUT /tickets/:id/assignee`. Only active tickets can change assignment. The store
+records both assignment and unassignment as `ticket.assigned`; assigning to an agent queues a `ticket.assigned`
+notification with an outbox key that includes that agent, while unassigning is silent. Listing filters combine with AND,
+and `assignee=` selects unassigned tickets.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The API, audit history, persistent ticket records and operator output include the assignment.
+- Older data files remain readable and receive `assignee: null` when loaded.
+- Each actual assignment to an agent can be retried through the existing outbox worker without losing a notification to
+  another agent assigned the same ticket later.
